        <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;">The festival</h2>
        <p class="body-copy">EXPRMNTL was an international festival for experimental film, established by Jacques Ledoux and the Royal Belgian Film Archive, co-organized with Pierre Vermeylen. Held in a vacant casino in Knokke-le-Zoute between Christmas and New Year, it ran for only five editions — 1949, 1958, 1963, 1967 and 1974 — yet became one of the few meeting points for avant-garde filmmakers from across the world, and is widely regarded as the most important event ever organized for experimental cinema.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;">This project</h2>
        <p class="body-copy">This site gathers photographs, programmes and digitized documents related to the festival into a single, browsable collection. It is a work in progress: most sections currently hold placeholder structure rather than final material, and are being filled in as items are digitized, catalogued and verified.</p>
